    "notes": "1. For total_revenue, the sum of 'Sales and other operating revenue', 'Income from equity affiliates', and 'Other income' equals the reported 'Total revenues and other income'.\n2. For total_operating_cost, the following line items from the 'Costs and other deductions' section are included as they represent the standard operating costs for an integrated oil & gas company: cost of goods sold (Crude oil and product purchases), production/manufacturing costs, SG&A, depreciation/depletion/impairment, exploration expenses, and non-service pension/postretirement costs. 'Other taxes and duties' and 'Interest expense' are excluded as they are reported separately.\n3. 'Other taxes and duties' is excluded from total_operating_cost as it is a separate tax line not directly tied to cost of revenue or operating expenses in this statement's presentation. It is also not included in the 'taxes' field, which is reserved for income tax expense.\n4. 'Net income' uses the line attributable to the parent company, 'Net income (loss) attributable to ExxonMobil'.\n5. 'Interest expense' is reported as a positive number as it reduces income.\n6. Supplementary tables for reserves and future cash flows are not directly mappable to income statement line items and are therefore not included in the extracted values.",
